The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms showing the impact of Nano-11 nanoparticles on the expression of costimulatory molecules (CD40, CD80, CD86) on dendritic cells (DCs). The black lines represent DCs treated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11, while the gray lines indicate medium control. Nano-11 treatment significantly increased the expression of CD80 and CD86, evidenced by a distinct rightward shift in their respective histograms, suggesting DC activation. The expression of CD40 showed a milder increase. This finding, described in Figure 6 of the PDF, supports Nano-11's ability to activate DCs, which is crucial for enhancing the immune response as a vaccine adjuvant.